  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "cm",
  "description": "The book's own example for 6.5 আপেক্ষিক তাপ: 10 kg of gold (s = 230) and 10 kg of water (s = 4200) on one stove. One tap gives both the same heat (42,000 J) and two thermometers on one scale show the gold rising about 18 K while the water rises 1 K. The panel works s = Q/m(T2 − T1) and C = ms from the readings, with the rule in the book's words, then a five-question test.",
